{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>You lift me to the wind</b> — All night long in my thoughts You make my soul ride upon things, and the תושיה, which is like wisdom, You melt me as the hills melt. And in truth You have lifted me up in the wind and made me ride, for <b>You melt me</b> is the opposite of <b>You make me ride</b>."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:03.894874560Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}